From 5558b8bf927d01f09c47eb94ead34b06ce5831c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:40:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 250/251] DOS-PORT: patch 0250 -- player journeys and stall
 share, next to fps

WHY: every figure this port gates on is a rate (fps_p50, tick_rate), and a
rate is an average: it cannot see a two-second room load, a slow save, a
click that took half a second to show, or one bad minute inside a good
run. The operator chose four journeys to watch beside fps (2026-09-23):
room transitions, save and load, click/key response, boot to title; plus
"stall share", the fraction of 1 s windows below 39 fps, and stalls over
100 ms per minute. Each has to be a real start and a real end the player
would recognise, on one clock, and it has to say when a journey FAILED
rather than quietly leaving it out of a percentile -- a p95 that improves
because the slow cases stopped finishing is worse than no p95.

WHAT: Engine/platform/dos/dos_journeys.{h,cpp}. Clock: uclock() from the
engine-start anchor (patch 0042). Every journey ends at a present ATTEMPT
(a scope guard on SDLRendererGraphicsDriver::Present, every exit: pixels
pushed, palette only, or skipped as unchanged). Starts: engine start
(boot; DOSAGS_JOURNEY_TITLE_ROOM picks the room that counts as the title);
NewRoom()/new_room() (room; ends after that room's fade-in); SaveGameSlot()
or save_game() (save; "written" is marked before GameSaved, whose script
work is not write time); RestoreGameSlot() or try_restore_save() (load;
ends at the first present not faded out and not fading in); the SDL
event's own timestamp (click/key; ends at the first present after the
engine dequeues it, with SDL 0220's upper bound on the unseen wait before
the poll). Failure is printed, not dropped: failed= (a failed or refused
save/load), unfinished=, superseded=, rerequested=, cleared=, and the
driver-vs-poll lost_clicks and IRQ-vs-drained keyboard bytes in
journey_input. Stall share counts present attempts per whole 1 s window
(floor DOSAGS_JOURNEY_FPS_FLOOR, default 39; empty seconds count as below;
a variant without windows that had a boot/room/save/load pending);
stalls100 lists present gaps over 100 ms and the tail from the last present
to quit. Nothing prints while the game runs; the record goes to
RUNMANI.LOG at quit. Cost: one uclock() and a flag test per present, O(1)
work per start/end event, 7 KB of .bss for 256 records. Permanent
reporting, not a probe: it has no switch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nz9XeKeVG8Ab7dm8esJsMu
